                        'heading' => 'A short history of concert pitch',
                        'body' => [
                            'Pitch has never stood still. Orchestras and organs in different cities tuned A anywhere from under 400 to over 460 Hz. In 1859 France fixed it at 435 Hz, the diapason normal. A conference in London in 1939 agreed on 440 Hz, and it became the international standard, ISO 16, in 1955.',
                            'Today most music is tuned to A440, many orchestras sit a little higher, and baroque players often use A415.',
