                    ],
                    [
                        'heading' => 'Pure and equal tuning, in cents',
                        'body' => [
                            'A cent is a hundredth of a semitone, and a piano spaces every semitone equally, so its intervals are whole hundreds: a fifth is 700 cents, a major third 400. A drone\'s pure intervals are the simple ratios its overtones line up on, and some sit noticeably off the piano\'s. A pure fifth is 701.96 cents and a pure major third 386.31; the table says how far each pure interval sits from the piano\'s.',
                        ],
