                            ],
                        ],
                    ],
                    [
                        'heading' => 'How a chord is voiced for four',
                        'body' => [
                            'A triad has three notes, so with four voices one is doubled: usually the root, which sounds most stable. The third is never left out, because it says whether the chord is major or minor; the fifth can be, when the lines need it.',
                            'In a seventh chord all four notes are sung, and the seventh is never doubled. It falls by step into the next chord, as G7\'s F falls to E in C.',
                        ],
                    ],
                    [
                        'heading' => 'Learning a part by ear',
                        'body' => [
