                        'heading' => 'The highest note matters most',
                        'body' => [
                            'Two songs with the same range can feel very different. One that touches its top note once is easy; one that sits near the top for a whole chorus wears you out. Look at where the melody spends its time, how long the high notes are held, and whether they land on your break.',
                            'The finder judges the lowest and highest notes, because those are the ones that decide whether you can sing it at all. Then trust your voice: sing a verse and the chorus in the key it gives, and move a semitone if it tires you.',
