                    [
                        'heading' => 'Guitar, duets and choirs',
                        'body' => [
                            'The guitar line uses the lowest capo, up to the 7th fret, that lets you play open chord shapes: C, G, D, A or E, or Am, Em or Dm in minor. So a song in E♭ becomes "capo 1, play D shapes". If the key is already an open one, it says so.',
                            'When a man sings a song first sung by a woman, or the other way round, an octave can sit too low or too high, so singers often move it a fourth or fifth instead: work out each voice separately. In a choir the key is set, and you find your part instead: the part whose range fits yours.',
                        ],
