                    [
                        'heading' => 'Harmonic intervals: two voices together',
                        'body' => [
                            'Together sings both notes at once, as two voices, which is how harmony sounds. Thirds and sixths blend sweetly, which is why so much harmony moves in them. Fourths, fifths and octaves sound open and hollow. Seconds, sevenths and the tritone rub and clash.',
                            'Harmonic intervals are harder to name at first, because you hear one sound rather than a step. Listen for the two notes inside it, and use Up to hear them apart when you\'re stuck.',
