                'faq' => [
                    ['What are the notes of a violin\'s strings?', 'G, D, A and E, from the lowest: G3, D4, A4 and E5. Each string is a fifth above the one below it.'],
                    ['Which violin string should I tune first?', 'The A, because it\'s the note orchestras tune to. Then tune the D, G and E, each against the A or its neighbour.'],
                    ['Can I tune a viola or cello here?', 'Yes. Open Settings and pick Viola (C, G, D, A, a fifth below the violin) or Cello (C, G, D, A, an octave below the viola).'],
                    ['Should I tune my violin to 440 or 442?', 'Use what your group uses. A440 is the standard; many orchestras tune a little higher, often to 442. Set it under More.'],
                    ['Why does the needle jump when I bow?', 'A bowed note starts with a scratchy attack. Play a long, even bow at a medium speed and read it once the note has settled, or pluck the string instead.'],
