                'faq' => [
                    ['What is 432 Hz tuning?', 'A tuning where the A above middle C is 432 Hz instead of the standard 440. Every note sits about a third of a semitone lower.'],
                    ['Is 432 Hz better, or healing?', 'There is no good evidence that it is. It\'s a matter of taste: some people like its slightly darker sound. What matters for playing together is that everyone uses the same A.'],
                    ['What is the difference between 432 Hz and 440 Hz?', '8 Hz on the A, which is 31.8 cents: about a third of a semitone. Strike both here, one after the other, to hear it.'],
                    ['How do I tune my instrument to 432 Hz?', 'Set your tuner\'s reference to 432 Hz (our tuner has it under More), or tune your A to this fork by ear and the other strings to it.'],
                    ['Is C256 the same as 432 Hz?', 'Close, but no. Middle C at A432 is 256.87 Hz, while C256 implies an A of about 430.5 Hz.'],
