                    ['How do I tune a guitar without a tuner?', 'Tune the low E to a reference, then use the 5th fret: the 6th string at the 5th fret gives the open A, the 5th string the open D, the 4th string the open G, and the 2nd string the open high E. The one exception is the G string, where the 4th fret gives the open B.'],
                    ['Can I tune an electric guitar with my phone?', 'Yes, unplugged: hold the phone close to the strings and pick firmly, because an electric guitar is quiet without an amp. Plugged into an amp, put the phone near the speaker.'],
                    ['Why does my guitar go out of tune?', 'New strings stretch for their first days, so keep retuning and they settle. Temperature, humidity and playing hard move the tuning too. Tune up to each note: if a string is sharp, go below the note and come back up, so the string holds.'],
