                        ['What are the inversions of a major chord?', 'The same three notes with a different one at the bottom: the root in root position, the third in first inversion, the fifth in second inversion. It\'s still the same major chord, but the lowest note changes how settled it feels, and second inversion usually feels the least settled.'],
