                    'lead' => 'A minor 7th chord is a minor chord with a minor seventh on top, a whole step below the octave. It sounds mellow and relaxed, softer than a plain minor chord.',
                    'guide' => [
                        [
                            'heading' => 'How it\'s built',
                            'body' => [
                                'Stack a minor third, a major third and another minor third: C, E♭, G and B♭. The top three notes make an E♭ major chord, so Cm7 has the same notes as E♭6. There\'s no semitone and no tritone anywhere in it, which is part of why it sounds so smooth.',
