                        ['What is the difference between a minor 7th and a dominant 7th chord?', 'The third. Both have a minor seventh, but the minor 7th has a minor third (E♭ over C) and the dominant 7th a major third (E). The minor 7th is mellow; the dominant 7th pulls toward the next chord.'],
                        ['Is Am7 the same as C6?', 'They have the same four notes, A, C, E and G, and the bass usually decides: with A at the bottom it acts as Am7, with C as C6. Tuned pure here, they even come out the same.'],
                        ['What is the difference between m7 and m7♭5?', 'The fifth. In m7♭5, the half-diminished chord, the fifth is lowered a semitone: C, E♭, G♭ and B♭. It sounds darker and less settled.'],
