                    'faq' => [
                        ['Why is it called half-diminished?', 'Because only half of it is diminished: the triad is, but the seventh is minor. A fully diminished 7th has a diminished seventh as well.'],
                        ['What does ø mean in a chord symbol?', 'Half-diminished: Cø7, Cø and Cm7♭5 all mean C, E♭, G♭ and B♭.'],
                        ['What is the difference between half-diminished and diminished 7th?', 'The seventh: a minor seventh in the half-diminished (B♭ over C), a diminished seventh in the diminished 7th (B𝄫, sounding as A). Half-diminished is the darker, gentler of the two.'],
                        ['Is Cm7♭5 the same as E♭m6?', 'They share the same four notes, C, E♭, G♭ and B♭. With C in the bass it\'s Cm7♭5; with E♭ there it acts as E♭m6.'],
