                    'faq' => [
                        ['What is the difference between add9 and sus2?', 'The third. An add9 keeps it, so it\'s still a major chord with a ninth on top: C, E, G and D. A sus2 drops the third for that same D: C, D and G, neither major nor minor.'],
                        ['What is the difference between add9 and a 9 chord?', 'A 9 chord has a seventh as well and an add9 doesn\'t. C9 is C, E, G, B♭ and D, a dominant 7th with a ninth; C add9 is C, E, G and D.'],
                        ['Is add9 the same as add2?', 'Nearly: they have the same notes. Add2 usually means the second sits close, next to the root or the third, and add9 that it sits above the octave, though many chord charts use the two names for the same thing.'],
