            ],
            'faq' => [
                ['Why warm up before singing?', 'A warm-up gets your breath, your voice and your ear working together before you ask them for a song. Gentle exercises like lip trills and humming ease the voice in, and short scales get you landing notes cleanly.'],
                ['How long should a vocal warm-up be?', 'For most singing, five to ten minutes is plenty. Start gently and low in effort, move to wider patterns, and stop well before your voice feels tired.'],
                ['Do I need a microphone or headphones?', 'No. The warm-ups play notes for you to sing with and nothing listens, so no microphone opens and a phone speaker is fine.'],
                ['What if the notes are too high or too low?', 'Pick a lower or higher voice, or under More choose how far it climbs. Each round moves a half step, so you can stop at any point and start again from the bottom.'],
