                'tie' => 'Your voice is warm. Now sing a harmony part.',
                'faq' => [
                    ['Why is humming a good warm-up?', 'Humming is gentle: the lips are closed and the sound is soft, so the voice warms up with very little effort. You can also feel the buzz of the sound, which tells you it is easy and not pushed.'],
                    ['Should I hum with my mouth closed?', 'Close your lips, but keep your teeth apart. A loose jaw and a tongue resting low give the hum room inside your mouth.'],
                    ['How loud should I hum?', 'Softly, about as loud as quiet talking. A loud hum pushes; keep it easy, and stop if anything tightens or scratches.'],
                    ['Can I hum instead of doing lip trills?', 'Yes. If your lips won\'t trill, humming is just as gentle a start.'],
