                'history' => [
                    'title' => 'Where the blues comes from',
                    'body' => [
                        'The blues is African American music. It took shape in the Deep South in the generation after slavery, out of work songs, field hollers, spirituals and ballads, and was sung for years before anyone printed it. Blues sheet music began in 1908, and the first blues songs were printed in 1912, by Black and white songwriters drawing on what Black singers were already singing. In the 1920s Black women singers brought it to records. A printing is one version of a song that lived in many.',
                        'The blues isn\'t only sad: it is also how people sang their way out of sadness.',
                    ],
